WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.168
-Today is Friday.

00:00:02.168 --> 00:00:04.070
And that's usually when I
catch up on some personal stuff.

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:06.606
You know, I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:06.606 --> 00:00:08.140
and of course I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:09.642
It's Friday. So, I was --

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:12.312
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.312 --> 00:00:13.746
I was running a bit behind,

00:00:13.746 --> 00:00:15.048
so I thought
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:15.048 --> 00:00:17.116
I'd just like to write out
my weekly thank-you notes

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:18.451
right now.
Is that okay with you?

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.987
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.987 --> 00:00:22.388
I appreciate it.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.723
James, can I get some thank-you-
note-writing music, please?

00:00:24.723 --> 00:00:26.526
[ Wistful piano music playing ]

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:31.130
[ Laughter ]

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.765
[ Piano music stops ]

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:34.300
-Wow.
-Is he real or animatronic?

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.236
-I think it was
animatronic James.

00:00:36.236 --> 00:00:38.404
It's the one we got
from Chuck E. Cheese.

00:00:38.404 --> 00:00:42.074
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.074 --> 00:00:43.676
-We got him at Chuck E. Cheese?

00:00:43.676 --> 00:00:45.044
-At Chuck E. Cheese, yeah.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:46.913
James couldn't make it today.

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:50.617
[ Laughter ]

00:00:50.617 --> 00:00:52.284
[ Wistful piano music restarts ]

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.620
-Thank you, "F9" poster,

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.155
for looking like
the squad's facing

00:00:56.155 --> 00:00:58.290
their most dangerous
threat yet --

00:00:58.290 --> 00:00:59.993
gender reveal parties.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.027
[ Laughter ]

00:01:02.027 --> 00:01:04.364
[ Piano music stops, applause ]

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:09.401
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:01:09.401 --> 00:01:13.106
Thank you, Milwaukee Bucks
mascot Bango,

00:01:13.106 --> 00:01:15.908
for looking like one of the
reindeer who bullied Rudolph.

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.977
[ Piano music stops, laughter ]

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.312
"You'll never be able to --"

00:01:20.312 --> 00:01:22.114
-[ High-pitched honk ]

00:01:22.114 --> 00:01:23.149
"Rudolph!"

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.651
-"I don't want to be a dentist."

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.352
-"Hermey!

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.255
Bumbles bounce."

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:30.556
[ Piano music restarts ]

00:01:30.556 --> 00:01:32.758
-Thank you, "Loki," for showing

00:01:32.758 --> 00:01:34.894
that all it takes
to control a literal god

00:01:34.894 --> 00:01:37.864
is a $39 shock collar
from chewy.com.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:39.165
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.201
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.605
-Chewy.

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.939
♪♪

00:01:46.939 --> 00:01:48.941
-Thank you, 4th of July,

00:01:48.941 --> 00:01:52.011
for being the day we celebrate
America's independence

00:01:52.011 --> 00:01:53.546
and also try to convince our
dogs

00:01:53.546 --> 00:01:55.147
that the world isn't ending.

00:01:55.147 --> 00:01:56.716
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:01:56.716 --> 00:01:59.785
Go in the basement or something.

00:01:59.785 --> 00:02:01.454
"What is happening?"

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:04.190
-"You're going
to have to shoot him.

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:05.592
His back is broke."

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.193
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.193 --> 00:02:09.162
-What do you say, there,
Vice President?

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:11.564
-[ Laughing ] His back --
-"Well, then I...

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:15.201
took the revolver,
I put it in the dog's mouth."

00:02:15.201 --> 00:02:17.002
-'Cause his back was --
-Looked him in the eye.

00:02:17.002 --> 00:02:19.672
-He wasn't going to heal.

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:21.774
-Made sure he knew it was me
that was doing it.

00:02:21.774 --> 00:02:23.976
-What does this have to do

00:02:23.976 --> 00:02:26.112
with the punch line? Yeah.
-This is terrible.

00:02:26.112 --> 00:02:29.048
[ Laughter ]

00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:30.617
Not really a ha-ha joke.

00:02:30.617 --> 00:02:32.585
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:37.823
That's a terrible joke.

00:02:37.823 --> 00:02:39.091
♪♪

00:02:39.091 --> 00:02:41.160
Thank you, sunscreen,

00:02:41.160 --> 00:02:43.730
for not being called
"safety mayonnaise."

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.598
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.598 --> 00:02:47.433
"Honey, just put on
your safety mayonnaise.

00:02:47.433 --> 00:02:49.469
You don't want the sun --"

00:02:51.537 --> 00:02:52.838
♪♪

00:02:52.838 --> 00:02:55.675
Thank you, bug zappers,
for letting me chill out

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:58.277
to the relaxing sounds
of mosquitos dying.

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.413
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:03:02.381 --> 00:03:03.983
-[ Imitates zap ]

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.852
-[ Grumbles indistinctly ]

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:08.487
-"You killed me.

00:03:08.487 --> 00:03:09.989
My family's in there."

00:03:09.989 --> 00:03:12.458
[ Laughter ]

00:03:12.458 --> 00:03:14.226
"Help me."
-Then a bee hops in there,

00:03:14.226 --> 00:03:16.195
and it's like a good sizzle
for a couple minutes.

00:03:16.195 --> 00:03:17.396
-Yeah, a couple hour--

00:03:17.396 --> 00:03:19.031
-Let 'em fry. Let 'em fry.

00:03:19.031 --> 00:03:21.567
-Then you shove a dog in there.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.337
-And then, well,
dog's back was broken,

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:25.939
so we had to put the dog --

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.339
put the dog's face in there.

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:29.408
He still had
some life left to him.

00:03:29.408 --> 00:03:31.377
-Mr. Vice President,
we got to get going.

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:33.112
-No, I'm almost finished
with the joke.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:35.481
[ Laughter ]

00:03:35.481 --> 00:03:38.818
That dog was still moving
a little bit, I think.

00:03:38.818 --> 00:03:41.887
So we lit a fire to him
with gasoline.

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:43.089
[ Sniffs ]

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.323
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.323 --> 00:03:47.493
I was a little hungry.

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:50.196
I had just come from Popeye's,
not knowing what to order.

00:03:50.196 --> 00:03:51.864
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.864 --> 00:03:54.467
"Mr. President, I'm just going
to turn your microphone off.

00:03:54.467 --> 00:03:55.701
We've heard more than enough.
-The kids --

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:57.437
-We've heard more than enough.

00:03:57.437 --> 00:03:59.505
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:00.773
♪♪

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:03.743
Thank you,
wearing socks and sandals,

00:04:03.743 --> 00:04:06.879
for saying either I'm married,
or I will never be married.

00:04:06.879 --> 00:04:08.414
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.414 --> 00:04:09.916
One or the other.
-One of the two.

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.050
-One or the other.

00:04:11.050 --> 00:04:13.185
♪♪

00:04:13.185 --> 00:04:15.154
-Dealer's choice.

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:19.359
♪♪

00:04:19.359 --> 00:04:21.594
-Thank you, hotel shampoos,

00:04:21.594 --> 00:04:25.230
or as you're called after the
vacation is over, my shampoos.

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:27.700
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.969
No one's going to use them
anyway. Come on.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:34.440
-Oh, may I take a few of those?

00:04:34.440 --> 00:04:35.607
♪♪

00:04:35.607 --> 00:04:37.677
-Thank you, QR codes,

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.713
for looking like barcodes
that got blackout drunk.

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:43.082
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

